#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
bravia-ready — convert a movie library into files a Sony Bravia plays off USB.

    bravia-ready --list                 # show what would be done, touch nothing
    bravia-ready                        # convert everything not already done
    bravia-ready "Spy Game (2001)"      # convert one title (dir name or path)
    bravia-ready --limit 2              # work through the queue two films at a time

Target format (established by testing on an actual set, not from documentation):

    container   MP4 with +faststart
    video       H.264 — HEVC is refused outright
    audio       AAC-LC, 48 kHz, stereo — AC3 refused, 96 kHz plays silently
    subtitles   sidecar .srt in UTF-16LE — UTF-8 renders as boxes
    naming      Title (Year).mp4 + Title (Year).srt, identical basenames

Source files are read straight off the pCloud FUSE mount, encoded to a local
scratch directory, and only copied up to the destination once complete and
verified. Nothing partial ever lands in the destination, so an interrupted run
is resumed by simply running the command again.

Requires: ffmpeg, ffprobe. Uses VAAPI when /dev/dri/renderD128 is present.
"""

